<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast> a prov:SoftwareAgent;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "delphisci dataset-resolvability assessor (Grok 4.7)";
    prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/usesModel> <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7-high-fast>.
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7-high-fast> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/LanguageModel>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Grok 4.7";
    dc:identifier "grok-4.7-high-fast".
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/levin-2024-anthrobots-17--grok> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/LLMClaimAssessment>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Grok 4.7 on levin-2024-anthrobots-17: not-empirically-resolvable, resolvability 0.19";
    dc:description "Straight-line motion with mirror symmetry is a geometric description already covered by the symmetry measurements. Calling that pattern a recapitulation of animal bilateral organization, or a route into embryonic midplane formation, adds no observation that would distinguish it from ordinary mechanics of a ciliated spheroid. The statement is therefore not separable from its non-developmental reading.";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Proposed test with existing data: Bilateral symmetry of a straight-swimming spheroid is measurable, but 'recapitulating a fundamental property of wild-type species' and usefulness for studying embryonic midplanes do not state a result that would come out differently if the symmetry were only a physical consequence of moving in a line.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/assessmentType> "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/evidenceAgainst> "Any elongated swimmer looks bilaterally symmetric about its path.", "No homology, shared gene circuit or shared midplane mechanism is specified that could fail while the shape similarity remained.";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasConfidence> "0.7"^^xsd:double;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasScore> "0.192"^^xsd:double;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasVerdict> "not-empirically-resolvable".
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/levin-2024-anthrobots-17--grok--analysis-feasibility> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/LLMClaimAssessment>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Analysis feasibility of levin-2024-anthrobots-17 by Grok 4.7: 0.25";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0-analysis-feasibility>;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/assessmentType> "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0/analysis-feasibility";
